## WHEN THIS COMMAND IS APPROPRIATE

Extended thinking is ONLY worth its token cost for:
- System architecture with significant tradeoffs (multiple valid approaches with different long-term implications)
- Non-obvious debugging (error not immediately traceable from stack trace or logs)
- Security threat modeling (attack surface analysis, trust boundary decisions)
- Algorithm design with competing approaches (time/space/complexity tradeoffs)
- Multi-step refactoring with cascading dependency effects
- Any task where the wrong first answer causes significant rework

If the problem is straightforward, say so explicitly instead of using thinking tokens on simple CRUD or boilerplate.

